Which version of Nethack are you playing?
(If you don't know, you can check it with the v command.)
There was a known bug in 3.4.0 (same as C340-29 mentioned on the page
http://www.nethack.org/v340/bugs.html ) that sometimes caused this to
happen, but it is supposed to be fixed since 3.4.1.
And the newest version now is 3.4.2.

And I agree with Boudewijn: if a bug like this ruins your game, it's ok to
use the save file copy to get it fixed. Especially since you noticed there
was something wrong and didn't use it to gain any advantage.

BTW, save and bones files from 3.4.0 are compatible with 3.4.1, and files
from 3.4.1 are compatible with 3.4.2.
Technically 3.4.0 files should be compatible with 3.4.2 as well, but
there's a minor glitch in the version checking. If you compile the game
yourself, you can make 3.4.2 accept 3.4.0 files by changing the value of
VERSION_COMPATIBILITY defined in include/patchlevel.h to 0x03040000L

